{
  "$comment": [
    "The layer contract, in one place.",
    "",
    "A layer is a routing decision: it names where /kiwa-design writes a spec, which",
    "Layer 2 skill turns that spec into test code, where that code lands, and which",
    "--target values of /kiwa-test pull it in.",
    "",
    "Four SKILL.md files used to declare the --layer enum independently, and a fifth",
    "place held the routing. Nothing compared them, so deleting a package in #1804",
    "left routing behind, and three inconsistencies survived until #1810 read them",
    "side by side, where a routing row, an enum entry and a flag disagreed.",
    "",
    "",
    "scripts/rebuild-layer-routing.mjs renders this file into those skills. Editing",
    "the generated regions by hand is caught by --check. Add a layer here, never",
    "there.",
    "",
    "Column notes:",
    "  consumer_skill   the skill that reads the spec and writes test code. Always a",
    "                   directory under .claude/skills/.",
    "  backing_package  the library the generated test imports. null when the layer",
    "                   is served by a package outside npm instead, which is what",
    "                   backing_runtime_package names.",
    "                   These were one column until #1810; conflating them is why the",
    "                   earlier check skipped rows it should have read.",
    "  test_output      where consumer_skill writes. The contract for /kiwa-review's",
    "                   resolver. Six layers disagreed with their producer and four",
    "                   had no entry at all before this table.",
    "  targets          which /kiwa-test --target values run this layer. Derived from",
    "                   the Step headings, not from the prose describing them; the two",
    "                   disagree today and #1809 decides which one moves.",
    "  mode             the framework a layer pins. null on every layer today: the six",
    "                   that carried a value were the Rust and Go framework layers and",
    "                   #1864 removed them. The column stays because kiwa layers --json",
    "                   mirrors this file, and dropping the key there is a different",
    "                   statement to a reader than keeping it null.",
    "",
    "A layer is listed only when the skill it names can actually serve it. A routing row without an enum entry, or an enum entry whose consumer implements neither the layer nor the flag the row advertises, would offer an option nothing can serve. The table records what works.",
    "",
    "providers vs variants: providers are the values a consumer accepts on its own --provider flag, which is only auth, job-queue and cache. variants are alternatives chosen some other way -- contract picks foundry or hardhat through kiwa-test --runner, and orm-query's three ORMs are read out of the spec with no flag at all. They were one column until review asked whether the values were really flags; writing them into providers claimed an interface that does not exist.",
    "",
    "targets records which --target values actually start a Step, not which ones the prose claims. Assigning them by runtime, as a first pass did, describes an intent rather than the behaviour.",
    "",
    "test_outputs is keyed by consumer because one layer can have more than one. contract is written by kiwa-forge as *.t.sol and by kiwa-hardhat as *.test.cjs, and a single value silently dropped the Hardhat review path.",
    "",
    "Each consumer's output is a list because Step 5.5 moves generated tests from examples/ into tests/fixtures/, so the same test lives in one of two places depending on whether that move has run. The original resolver carried both and the first version of this table kept only the first, which would have made review miss every test already moved.",
    "",
    "The moved form keeps the name the generator gave the file -- Step 5.5 is a git mv into another directory, not a rename. So its basename is whatever the producer wrote and cannot be derived from the example. e2e declared tests/fixtures/{example}/e2e-test/{example}.spec.ts and matched zero files in all five fixtures (mint-nft holds mint.spec.ts, defi-swap holds swap.spec.ts), which read as 'this example has no e2e test' rather than as a wrong declaration. A moved form names the basename with a wildcard unless the producer is known to derive it from the example."
  ],
  "specRoot": "tests/spec",
  "layers": [
    {
      "id": "contract",
      "spec_dir": "contract",
      "spec_path": "tests/spec/contract/test-spec-{module}.md",
      "runtime": "solidity",
      "consumer_skill": "kiwa-forge",
      "also_consumed_by": [
        "kiwa-hardhat"
      ],
      "backing_package": null,
      "backing_runtime_package": null,
      "providers": [],
      "mode": null,
      "targets": [
        "contract",
        "both"
      ],
      "variants": [
        "foundry",
        "hardhat"
      ],
      "selected_by": "kiwa-test --runner {foundry|hardhat|both}",
      "test_outputs": {
        "kiwa-forge": [
          "{example}/test/*.t.sol",
          "tests/fixtures/{example}/contract-test/{Contract}.t.sol"
        ],
        "kiwa-hardhat": [
          "{example}/test/*.test.ts",
          "tests/fixtures/{example}/hardhat-test/{Contract}.test.cjs"
        ]
      }
    },
